# .github/CODEOWNERS — declared ownership map (issue #1073).
#
# This is a single-owner repo today, so every rule below resolves to the same
# owner. The value of this file is the DECLARED map, not the owner diversity:
# it names one rule per pillar/cross-cutting directory (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md,
# AGENTS.md) so a reviewer requirement can later be attached per area without
# discovering the boundaries from scratch, and so `scripts/check-codeowners.sh`
# has something concrete to hold to the tree (every pillar dir present, every
# rule naming a path that exists, no stale entries).
#
# A second owner is added PER RULE, as an area gains a distinct reviewer, and
# is NEVER added via the default (`*`) line — the default stays the fallback
# owner for anything not named below, not a blanket second reviewer for every
# pillar.
#
# GitHub reads the LAST matching rule, so the default comes first and every
# more specific rule follows it.

# Default owner — fallback for anything not matched below.
*                 @kushin77

# Five-pillar architecture (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
/registry/        @kushin77
/gateway/         @kushin77
/engine/          @kushin77
/guardrails/      @kushin77
/telemetry/       @kushin77

# Cross-cutting tenant identity/RBAC, control-plane/portal, autonomous
# ops/governance.
/identity/        @kushin77
/control-plane/   @kushin77
/portal/          @kushin77
/governance/      @kushin77

# Infrastructure, tooling, docs, CI-adjacent config, fleet automation.
/infra/           @kushin77
